Recipe "daynight" for this kit3d.js game: a day and night cycle (one day is 90 seconds): the sky and lights darken at night; g.night is true at night, so other code can spawn more enemies then.
Paste each part into game.js with file_edit. It uses g.player.

--- 1. top of game.js, after the other let/const lines ---
const DAY = 90;
let clock = 0;
const daySky = new THREE.Color('#9fd3f5'), nightSky = new THREE.Color('#0b1324');

--- 2. inside init(g), at the end (after g.player is made) ---
clock = 0;

--- 3. inside update(g, dt), at the end ---
clock += dt;
const sunUp = 0.5 + 0.5 * Math.cos((clock / DAY) * Math.PI * 2); // 1 at noon, 0 at midnight
g.night = sunUp < 0.3;
Kit.sun.intensity = 0.2 + 2 * sunUp;
Kit.hemi.intensity = 0.25 + 1.05 * sunUp;
const sky = nightSky.clone().lerp(daySky, sunUp);
Kit.scene.background = sky;
if (Kit.scene.fog) Kit.scene.fog.color.copy(sky);
Kit.hud(g.night ? 'Night' : 'Day', 'time');

